    <task><title>Part 1: Evaluate the limit</title>
<statement><p>Evaluate the following limit by simplifying the expression (first answer box) and then evaluating the limit (second answer box).</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \lim_{x\to -6} {\frac{x^{2}-36}{x+6}} = \lim_{x\to -6} }</m> <fillin characters="7" name="AnSwEr0001"/> <m>\displaystyle{= }</m> <fillin characters="6" name="AnSwEr0002"/>.</p>
<p>Note: In your written solution, you should write the limit statement <m>\displaystyle{\lim_{x \to -6}}</m> in every step except the last one, where the limit is finally evaluated.</p>
</statement><answer><p><m>x-6</m></p></answer><answer><p><m>-12</m></p></answer></task>
    <task><title>Part 2: Follow-up question</title>
<statement><p>Select the true statement</p>
<p><var form="buttons">
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle \frac{x^{2}-36}{x+6} = x-6</m> for all <m>x \not= -6</m>.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle \frac{x^{2}-36}{x+6} = x-6</m> for all <m>x</m>.</p>
</li>
</var></p>
</statement></task>
